  "statement": "Find the first three terms in the expansion of $(1-2x)^{3/2}$ in ascending powers of $x$.",
  "solution": "$(1+u)^{3/2}=1+\\\\tfrac32u+\\\\tfrac{3/2\\\\cdot1/2}{2}u^{2}+\\\\cdots=1+\\\\tfrac32u+\\\\tfrac38u^{2}+\\\\cdots$. With $u=-2x$: $1+\\\\tfrac32(-2x)+\\\\tfrac38(4x^{2})=1-3x+\\\\tfrac32x^{2}$.",
